Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||08-24-2001||09:05 PM||||Well, I had some trouble today with the EGR, checked it out and saw that the tube was broke on it.  I need my car for every day use at this time, so I need some ideas fast on what I can do.  Do they even sell these tubes at bumper to bumper or Napa?  See pics.<P>Here is the tube.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P8240001.JPG"> <P>And here is where it broke.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P8240003.JPG"> <P>I need one by tomorrow morning!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||AL||08-24-2001||09:48 PM||||just buy a regular vac hose and connect it,just cause it's plastic it don't mean you can't put rubber hoses on it,i changed out all my plastic lines with good old rubber, to much of a headache trying to fixs plastic,your local autoparts carry's it.<BR><B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <BR>84 Indy 4 speed (stole it)250$<BR>86 GT rebuilt it<BR>89 ws6GTA<P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
